<section class="page-hero page-hero--legal">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--center">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="page-hero__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="page-hero__lead">
      This policy explains what information <%= site.name %> collects, how your files are
      handled, and the choices you have. In short: your documents are processed in your
      browser and are not uploaded to our servers.
    </p>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: <%= lastUpdated %></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container prose legal">

    <div class="legal-summary">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul class="check-list">
        <li>Your files are opened and processed <strong>in your browser</strong>. We do not upload, view or store their contents.</li>
        <li>We do not require an account to use the tools.</li>
        <li>We don’t set analytics or advertising cookies; if that ever changes, we’ll ask for your consent first.</li>
        <li>If advertising is enabled, ad partners such as Google may use cookies — you control this through the cookie banner.</li>
        <li>You can contact us anytime at <a href="mailto:<%= site.privacyEmail %>"><%= site.privacyEmail %></a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      <%= site.name %> (“we”, “us”, “our”) provides a free, browser-based toolkit for working
      with PDFs and documents. This policy applies to our website and the in-browser editor.
      For any privacy question, email <a href="mailto:<%= site.privacyEmail %>"><%= site.privacyEmail %></a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. How your files are handled</h2>
    <p>
      <%= site.name %> is a client-side application. When you open a file in a tool, that file
      is read and processed <strong>locally on your device, inside your web browser</strong>.
      Your document’s contents are <strong>not transmitted to our servers</strong>, and we do
      not receive, view, store or share them.
    </p>
    <p>
      While you work, a copy of your document lives in your browser’s memory. To handle larger
      files, the app may temporarily use your browser’s own on-device storage (such as the
      Origin Private File System) — this data stays on your device. When you close or refresh
      the tab, the working copy is discarded. Any exported file is saved directly to the
      location you choose on your own device.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because we never receive your files, we cannot recover them for you and we do not keep
      backups of them. We do not claim that files are “automatically deleted from our servers,”
      because your files are never on our servers in the first place.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Information we do collect</h2>
    <p>We keep data collection to a minimum. Depending on how you use the site, this may include:</p>
    <ul class="check-list check-list--muted">
      <li>
        <strong>Server access logs.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting infrastructure may
        record standard technical information when you load a page — such as your IP address,
        browser type, referring page and the time of the request. This is used to operate,
        secure and troubleshoot the service.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Messages you send us.</strong> If you email us or use the contact form (which
        opens your email app), we receive the details you provide — such as your name, email
        address and message — so we can respond.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cookie and consent preferences.</strong> We store your cookie choice in your
        browser so we can respect it on future visits.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information, and we do not build advertising
      profiles about you ourselves.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      We use a small amount of browser storage to make the site work and to remember your
      preferences. Where cookies are not strictly necessary, we ask for your consent first.
      For full details, see our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We do not currently use third-party analytics or tracking services to profile visitors.
      If we introduce privacy-respecting analytics in the future, we will update this policy and
      our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a>, and — where required — request your consent first.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
    <p>
      We may display advertising to help keep <%= site.name %> free. When advertising is enabled,
      we intend to use Google AdSense. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve
      ads based on a user’s prior visits to this and other websites.
    </p>
    <ul class="check-list check-list--muted">
      <li>Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you.</li>
      <li>
        You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
        <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        You can also opt out of some third-party vendors’ use of cookies for personalised
        advertising at
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">aboutads.info/choices</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Learn how Google uses information from sites that use its services at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom or Switzerland, we will ask
      for your consent before non-essential advertising cookies are set, and you can withdraw it
      at any time using the cookie banner.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>We rely on a small number of third parties to run the site:</p>
    <ul class="check-list check-list--muted">
      <li><strong>Hosting provider</strong> — serves the website and may process server access logs on our behalf.</li>
      <li><strong>Google AdSense</strong> — advertising, when enabled (see section 6).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Fonts and application code are served from our own domain, so using the site does not, by
      itself, send requests to third-party font or code networks.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      We do not store your documents, so there is nothing for us to retain there. Server access
      logs are kept only as long as needed for security and operational purposes. Messages you
      send us are kept for as long as needed to handle your request and any follow-up.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR or CCPA/CPRA), you may have the
      right to access, correct, delete or restrict the processing of personal information we hold
      about you, to object to certain processing, and to lodge a complaint with a supervisory
      authority. Because we hold very little personal data, most requests relate to messages you
      have sent us. To exercise any right, email
      <a href="mailto:<%= site.privacyEmail %>"><%= site.privacyEmail %></a>.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      <%= site.name %> is not directed to children, and we do not knowingly collect personal
      information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal data,
      please contact us and we will address it.
    </p>

    <h2>11. International users</h2>
    <p>
      The site can be accessed globally. Where server logs or messages are processed, they may be
      handled in the country where our hosting provider operates. By using the site you understand
      that this limited technical information may be processed in those locations.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as the service evolves or as legal requirements change. When we do,
      we will revise the “Last updated” date above. Significant changes will be highlighted on the
      site where appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data? Email
      <a href="mailto:<%= site.privacyEmail %>"><%= site.privacyEmail %></a> or visit our
      <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
    </p>

  </div>
</section>
